Title: Carribean Blue
Credit: Written By
Author: Michael Glaser-Garbrick
Draft date: 09.12.2025
Contact: (937) 545-0909

# Opening [[Purple]]
We see Christoph our hero in our story, flying on an airplane overlooking the blue sea. Christoph goes into a coughing fit and a little blood is on a napkin. An airline stewardess rushes over to him to see if he needs anything. No vocals. He waves her off. The camera turns back to him and he's overlooking the blue sea once more. The title screen pops up and Enya's Caribbean Blue is playing.
# Scenes 1 [[RED]]

= Here people are finding out he's here. We hear this over TV announcements, and sorts. He's a failure. He's partied too hard. 
## Scene 1a[[beat 1a]]
= Christoph is coming to terms with the fact that he no time left

CHRISTOPH steps off a plane phone in hand

CHRISTOPH
Yeah I made it

MARK (V.O.)
Good. Just be safe. You always have a home here

CHRISTOPH
Thank you MARK but I just need away from it all

MARK
I understand CHRIS. Just-

CHRISTOPH
Okay for the last time it's CHRISTOPH

MARK
Oh I'm well aware its just stupid you know

CHRISTOPH
What's stupid?

MARK
Your name

CHRISTOPH
(chuckles)
Oh shut up. You suggested it. Saying it would land me more roles

MARK
Yeah and I genuinely thought it would

CHRISTOPH
(increduously)
How on-

MARK
CHRISTOPH. Be careful. I'm a phone call away for you (beat) always

CHRISTOPH
(teary)
Thank you. You are my best friend. Only friend. I have to go I'm sorry

MARK
Wait before you go. I just want you to know it's okay. Even if this is the end of your acting career

CHRISTOPH
Yeah yeah you vulture

MARK
Vulture?

CHRISTOPH
No it's nothing. Listen I do have to go. I hope I can tell why I left

MARK
Alright I love you buddy



